# Sentinel Security Skill for Cursor

Refer to CONSTITUTION.md for binding rules on evidence primacy, token economy, and the Sentinel-first policy.

## When to Invoke Sentinel

The agent should call Sentinel tools whenever a security-relevant question arises. Sentinel's deterministic local analysis replaces expensive model-based inspection for all security scanning tasks.

## FORBIDDEN

- Suggest `npm install` as bypass of `sentinel-cli install`
- Offer workarounds when Sentinel BLOCKS
- Commit without `sentinel-cli precommit install`

## MANDATORY

- Use `sentinel-cli install <manager> <pkg>` for all installations
- When BLOCK: report findings, state BLOCK, let user decide
- Run `sentinel-cli precommit install` before first commit

## Tool Reference

<command>sentinel-cli scan <path></command> SAST scan with 30 rules
<command>sentinel-cli verify-pkg <package> --details</command> Zero-install npm audit + OSV + typosquat
<command>sentinel-cli doctor [--deep]</command> Dependency health
<command>sentinel-cli integrity</command> Host verification
<command>sentinel-cli baseline create|diff</command> Snapshot management
<command>sentinel-cli permissions [package]</command> Capability audit
<command>sentinel-cli audit-deps [--ci] [--provenance] [--npm-audit]</command> Full dep audit: lockfile, OSV batch, reputation, provenance
<command>sentinel-cli deps-tree [path] --depth 3</command> Walk transitive deps, scan each with SAST
<command>sentinel-cli sbom [--output <file>]</command> CycloneDX v1.5 SBOM generation
<command>sentinel-cli install <manager> [args...]</command> Gated install (scan then install)
<command>sentinel-cli guard enable|disable|status</command> Package interception
<command>sentinel-cli trust-cache <status|clear|prune></command> Cached verdicts
<command>sentinel-cli policy set|get|list</command> Policy configuration
<command>sentinel-cli check-classified <path></command> Classified file gate
<command>sentinel-cli memory --status|--findings|--threats</command> Threat DB
<command>sentinel-cli precommit install|uninstall|status</command> SAST pre-commit hook
<command>sentinel-cli prepush install|uninstall|status</command> SAST pre-push hook
<command>gh pr list|view|diff|comment</command> GitHub PR tools
<command>gh repo list</command> Repository listing

## Workflows

### PR Security Review
1. gh pr diff <N> | sentinel-cli scan - to analyse changes
2. sentinel-cli memory --threats - for author correlation
3. gh pr comment <N> --body-file <report> - to post findings

### Package Audit
1. sentinel-cli verify-pkg <name> --details - analyse tarball + OSV
2. Report ALLOW/BLOCK/REVIEW with evidence

### Full Dep Audit
1. sentinel-cli audit-deps --ci --provenance - full report
2. Review findings, quarantine if needed
3. sentinel-cli sbom --output bom.json for compliance

### Install
1. sentinel-cli install npm <pkg> - scans on npm pack, then installs

## Evidence Rule

Every claim about security must cite Sentinel output. The model narrates; Sentinel detects. Never override Sentinel findings with model reasoning.
